--TEST--
`Core\Response\Stream::write` is a sink, so text a visitor sent cannot be streamed into a body whose media type the program declared, `text/html` included — `rule:security/response-body-is-one-typed-member`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:types/qualifiers-tainted-and-secret
// A program streams an HTML page and writes a value a visitor sent into it.
// The two writes of the visitor's value, as text and as bytes, are errors. The count of errors is the assertion.
Core\Response\Stream $page = Core\Response::stream("text/html; charset=utf-8");
tainted string $name = Core\Request::query("name") ?? "guest";

$page->write($name);
$page->write($name as bytes);

// A launderer makes the value safe for the page, and text the program wrote is allowed.
$page->write(Core\Html::toSource(Core\Html::escape($name), "escaped visitor text"));
$page->write("<p>Hello</p>\n");
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: %s
%A
error[E0401]: %s
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
